<title>USA: Harris faces $15.4 mln patent judgment.</title>
<headline>Harris faces $15.4 mln patent judgment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Comark Communications Inc said Thursday a federal judge affirmed an earlier jury finding that Harris Corp's broadcast unit infringed on Comark's patent for a device which corrects audio distortions in television transmitters.</p>
<p>Harris said the judge doubled the jury recommendation to a $15.4 million award, but it planned to appeal.</p>
<p>&quot;We have already told the court we disagree with the judgment and will appeal to a federal circuit court of appeals,&quot; Jim Burke, a Harris spokesman said.</p>
</text>
